le"}],"gloss":"who lost"},{"surface":"யான்","parts":[{"text":"யான்","lemma":"யான்","gloss":"I"}],"gloss":"I"},{"surface":"ஒன்றோ","parts":[{"text":"ஒன்று","lemma":"ஒன்று","gloss":"one"},{"text":"ஓ","lemma":"ஓ","gloss":"emphasis"}],"gloss":"not only that"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"மன்பதை","parts":[{"text":"மன்பதை","lemma":"மன்பதை","gloss":"mankind"}],"gloss":"mankind"},{"surface":"காக்கும்","parts":[{"text":"கா","lemma":"கா","gloss":"protect"},{"text":"க்கும்","lemma":"க்கும்","gloss":"habitual relative participle"}],"gloss":"protecting"},{"surface":"நீள்குடிச்","parts":[{"text":"நீள்","lemma":"நீள்","gloss":"long"},{"text":"குடி","lemma":"குடி","gloss":"lineage"},{"text":"ச்","lemma":"ச்","gloss":"sandhi"}],"gloss":"ancient lineage"},{"surface":"சிறந்த","parts":[{"text":"சிறந்த","lemma":"சிற","gloss":"excellent"}],"gloss":"excellent"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"தென்புலம்","parts":[{"text":"தென்புலம்","lemma":"தென்புலம்","gloss":"southern land"}],"gloss":"southern land"},{"surface":"காவலின்","parts":[{"text":"காவல்","lemma":"காவல்","gloss":"protection"},{"text":"இன்","lemma":"இன்","gloss":"from"}],"gloss":"from protecting"},{"surface":"ஒரிஇப்","parts":[{"text":"ஒரிஇ","lemma":"ஒருவு","gloss":"abandon"},{"text":"ப்","lemma":"ப்","gloss":"sandhi"}],"gloss":"having abandoned"},{"surface":"பிறர்","parts":[{"text":"பிறர்","lemma":"பிறர்","gloss":"others"}],"gloss":"others"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"வன்புலங்","parts":[{"text":"வன்புலங்","lemma":"வன்புலங்","gloss":"hard land"}],"gloss":"hard land","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"காவலின்","parts":[{"text":"காவல்","lemma":"காவல்","gloss":"protection"},{"text":"இன்","lemma":"இன்","gloss":"of"}],"gloss":"of protecting"},{"surface":"மாறி","parts":[{"text":"மாறி","lemma":"மாறு","gloss":"change"}],"gloss":"having changed"},{"surface":"யான்","parts":[{"text":"யான்","lemma":"யான்","gloss":"I"}],"gloss":"I"},{"surface":"பிறக்கே","parts":[{"text":"பிறக்கே","lemma":"பிறக்கே","gloss":"may I be born"}],"gloss":"may I be born","split_unverified":true}]}],"literal":"Like a lion having become angry, with an unyielding heart, / unsubmissive army kings, together agreeing, / 'with me they will clash' they say, them / fierce battle to scream having attacked, with chariot / their backs I do not see if, excellent / large beautiful kohl-painted eyes her even from may I separate! / Righteousness state to deviate, without love in the court, / ability-less one person having seated, justice having deviated, / cruel sceptre rule I did may I become! Abundant fame / River Vaiyai surrounded, victory possessing region's / unfailing new wealth Maiyal chief, / Mavan and, enduring fortress Anthai and, worthy of praise / Anthuvan Sathan and, Athan Azhisi and, / fierce anger Iyakkan and, including others, / eye like friendship with friends mingled / sweet joy delight laughter who lost I, not only that, / mankind protecting ancient lineage excellent / southern land protection from having abandoned, others' / hard land protection of instead, may I be born!","translation":"They say those kings of unsubmissive armies, agreeing together with unyielding hearts like angry lions, will clash with me. If I do not attack them in fierce battle making them scream, and see their backs fleeing with their chariots, may I be parted from her of the large, beautiful, kohl-painted eyes! May I become one who deviates from righteousness, seats an incompetent man in a court devoid of love, and rules with a cruel sceptre! May I lose the sweet joy, delight, and laughter shared with friends as dear as my own eyes—Mavan, the chief of Maiyal with its unfailing wealth surrounded by the Vaiyai river, Anthai of the enduring fortress, the praiseworthy Anthuvan Sathan, Athan Azhisi, and the fiercely angry Iyakkan, along with others! Not only that, may I be cast out from protecting the southern land, a duty of my ancient lineage that protects mankind, and instead be born to protect the harsh lands of others!","modern":"கோபமடைந்த சிங்கத்தைப் போல வளைந்து கொடுக்காத நெஞ்சமும், அடங்காத படைகளும் கொண்ட பகை வேந்தர்கள் ஒன்று கூடி, 'என்னோடு போரிடுவோம்' என்று கூறுகிறார்கள். அவர்களைக் கொடிய போர்க்களத்தில் அலற அலறத் தாக்கி, அவர்களின் தேர்களோடு அவர்கள் முதுகு காட்டி ஓடுவதை நான் காணாவிட்டால், சிறந்த பெரிய மை தீட்டிய கண்களைக் கொண்ட என் மனைவியைப் பிரிந்து போவேனாக! அறநெறி தவறி, இரக்கமில்லாத அவையிலே தகுதியற்ற ஒருவனை அமர்த்தி, முறை தவறி கொடுங்கோல் ஆட்சி செய்தவன் ஆவேனாக! வையை ஆறு சூழ்ந்த, வளம் மிக்க வஞ்சியம்பதியின் தலைவனான பொய்யா யாணர் மையற் கோமான் மாவன், நிலைபெற்ற மதிலையுடைய ஆந்தை, புகழ்பெற்ற அந்துவஞ் சாத்தன், ஆதன் அழிசி, வெஞ்சினமுடைய இயக்கன் ஆகியோருடனும், என் கண் போன்ற பிற நண்பர்களடனும் கூடி மகிழ்ந்திருந்த இனிய மகிழ்ச்சியையும் சிரிப்பையும் இழந்தவன் ஆவேனாக! அதுமட்டுமன்றி, மக்களைக் காக்கும் நீண்ட குடிப்பெருமை வாய்ந்த தென்புலத்தைக் காக்கும் பொறுப்பிலிருந்து நீங்கி, பிறருடைய வன்புலத்தைக் காக்கும் எளியவனாக நான் பிறப்பேனாக!","explanation":"This poem is a famous oath (vañciṉam) taken by the Pandya king Ollaiyūr Tanta Pūtappāṇṭiyaṉ. When rival kings mock his youth and unite to attack him, the king swears a solemn oath detailing the terrible consequences he wishes upon himself if he fails to defeat them. He swears that if he does not make them flee, he should be separated from his beloved wife, become a tyrant who rules unjustly, lose the company of his dearest friends (whom he names individually), and lose his royal lineage's right to rule the fertile southern Pandya kingdom, instead being reborn to serve in harsh, foreign lands. The poem belongs to the puram genre, specifically the kāñci tiṇai and vañciṉak kāñci tuṟai, which deals with a king taking a vow of vengeance before battle. The vivid imagery of his loyal friends and his deep love for his wife contrasts sharply with the harshness of the battlefield, highlighting the immense stakes of his honor. Key words include maṭaṅkal (lion), vañciṉam (oath), teṉpulam (southern land/Pandya country), and kēḷir (friends).","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"}}